     A token that contains any of the characters ?, *, or [ is a
     file-name pattern: ?  matches any one character, * matches
     any string of characters (including none), and [_c_h_a_r_s]
     matches any one of the enclosed characters (a range may be
     written _c_1- _c_2). sshh replaces such a token with the sorted
     list of file names in the current directory that match it;
     if none match, the token is passed through unchanged.  A
     leading .  in a file name, and every /, must be matched ex-
     plicitly.

     The characters \, ', and quote (turn off the special meaning
     of) other characters.    \ quotes the single character that
     follows it; a \ immediately followed by a newline is dis-
     carded, letting a command be continued onto the next line.
     A pair of single quotes (' ... ') quotes everything between
     them.  A pair of double quotes (" ... ") also quotes every-
     thing between them, except that $ substitutions (below)
     still occur inside them.

     A token of the form $_n_a_m_e, ${_n_a_m_e}, or $_n (a single digit _n,
     1 through 9) is replaced by the value of the shell variable
     _n_a_m_e or of positional parameter _n. The forms ${_n_a_m_e-_w_o_r_d},
     ${_n_a_m_e=_w_o_r_d}, ${_n_a_m_e+_w_o_r_d}, and ${_n_a_m_e?_w_o_r_d} substitute _w_o_r_d
     if _n_a_m_e is unset (and, for =, also assign it _w_o_r_d); +
     substitutes _w_o_r_d only if _n_a_m_e _i_s set; and ?  substitutes
     _w_o_r_d (or a default message) and aborts the shell if _n_a_m_e is
     unset.  The following special parameters are also recog-
     nized:

          $00   The name the shell was invoked with.

          $#   The number of positional parameters.

          $*   All positional parameters.

          $@   All positional parameters; inside double quotes,
               each becomes a separate word.

          $-   The options currently in effect.

          $?   The exit status of the last command.



