CCOOMMMMAANNDD-LLIINNEE OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     -cc _c_m_d_s
          Read commands from the following argument, _c_m_d_s, in-
          stead of from a file or the standard input.

     -ee   If the shell is not interactive, exit as soon as any
          command returns a nonzero status or is not found.

     -ii   Treat the shell as interactive (print prompts, and ig-
          nore SSIIGGTTEERRMM and SSIIGGIINNTT) even if its input is not a
          terminal.

     -kk   Put all keyword (variable=value) arguments of a command
          into that command's environment, not just the ones that
          precede the command name.

     -nn   Read and parse commands but do not execute them; useful
          for checking a script's syntax.

     -ss   Read commands from the standard input even if file or
          -cc arguments are also given, and write ordinary output
          to the standard error.

     -tt   Read and execute a single command, then stop.

     -uu   Treat the reference to an unset shell variable as an
          error, instead of substituting the null string.

     -vv   Echo each input line as it is read.

     -xx   Echo each command and its arguments, after substitu-
